{
  "model": "DULCOMETER diaLog DACa multi-parameter controller (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "dialog-daca",
  "short_model": "diaLog DACa",
  "aliases": [
    "DACa",
    "diaLog DACa",
    "DULCOMETER DACa"
  ],
  "applies_to": "diaLog DACa controllers with the Modbus RTU interface option, per software manual BA DM 212 12/15.",
  "summary": "The diaLog DACa is ProMinent's multi-parameter measuring and control controller; its register map has two measuring and control channels plus a calculated (mathematic) channel. With the Modbus RTU option it is an RS-485 or RS-232 slave. This map covers measured values, setpoints, status, warning and error words per channel, output states, device information, stop/pause commands and the per-channel control configuration (setpoints, limits, PID terms).",
  "source": {
    "title": "Software manual DULCOMETER Multi-parameter Controller diaLog DACa Modbus RTU",
    "doc_number": "984163 BA DM 212 12/15 EN",
    "revision_date": "2015-12",
    "url": "https://www.prominent.com/resources/OperatingInstructions/English/15023/984163-BA-DM-212-12-15-EN-Modbus-RTU-DACa-EN.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 5-10 (settings, commands, word order, numbering), pp. 11-17 (register table), pp. 19-24 (bit fields)"
  },
  "manufacturer": "ProMinent",
  "manufacturer_slug": "prominent",
  "equipment_type": "Sensor / multi-parameter controller",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Odd",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The manual prints a decimal 'Register' number plus the hex PDU address; the PDU address is the register minus 1 (register 100 is requested at PDU address 99, hex 63). The 'address' field here is the PDU address."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "notes": [
    "32-bit values (FLOAT32 and UINT32) put bits 31-16 in the first register and bits 15-0 in the second, so the word order is ABCD; bytes are sent high byte first. Register 198 (PDU 197) always reads 0xAABBCCDD as a check.",
    "Measured value, setpoint, limits and Xp are floats in whatever unit the channel is configured for (pH, mV, ppm and so on); the manual does not list units for them.",
    "Left out: Pump relay 4 (register 139), because its printed PDU address (hex 90) does not match register 139 (which would be hex 8A); the identity-code registers 150-161, because their text encoding is not described; the math-channel error registers 130/131, which the manual marks as reserved for later use; and channel 1 'Additive basic load' (215), printed as UINT16 although its range is -100 to +100 % (channels 2 and 3 are INT16).",
    "Channel 1 temperature is printed as INT16 and the other channels' temperature as UINT16; both are in 0.1 °C steps and are listed exactly as printed.",
    "Configuration word: the manual's listing of the control-type code (bits 3-6) is garbled in this edition, so only bits 0, 1, 14 and 15 are given here. The later DACb manual lists the codes cleanly.",
    "The table lists an 'Error confirmation channel 3' register (247) although DACa has two measuring channels; it is kept as printed."
  ],
